  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\alpha, \\beta$ be the roots of $x^2-a(x-1)+b=0$, then the value of $\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2-a \\alpha}+\\frac{1}{\\beta^2-a \\beta}+\\frac{2}{a+b}$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PTsg6",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{a+b}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VkPJI",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{a+b}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NmQ50",
      "text": "0",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iV2ea",
      "text": "-1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Hints }: x^2-a x=a+3 \\quad \\alpha \\beta=a+b \\\\\n& \\alpha+\\beta=a \\\\\n& \\alpha^2-a \\alpha=-(a+b) \\\\\n& \\beta^2-a \\alpha=-(a+b) \\\\\n&-\\frac{1}{a+b}-\\frac{1}{a+b}+\\frac{2}{a+b}=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
